              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "محو الأمية — maḥw al-ummiyya — \"literacy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تعمل الجمعية على محو الأمية في القرى. taʿmalu al-jamʿiyya ʿalā maḥw al-ummiyya fī al-qurā. The association works for literacy in the villages."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally the wiping out of illiteracy; أمي, ummī, is one who cannot read."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "محو الأمية (maḥw al-ummiyya) joins maḥw, \"wiping out\", built on the native Arabic root m-ḥ-w, and ummiyya, \"illiteracy\", from ummī, built on ʾ-m-m (Lane): one still as his mother bore him, unable to read."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
